WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.560
Hey there, welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners, episode 69 for June 12, 2026.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:10.500
Today's AI news is pretty exciting, and I promise, no jargon, let's go.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:15.880
Something wild just happened with your favorite food delivery app, DoorDash added a new chat

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:21.460
bot called Ask DoorDash that lets you order by typing normal sentences or even snapping

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.040
a photo.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.600
No more scrolling through endless restaurant lists and filters.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:31.080
Think of it like texting a friend who already knows every menu in your city and can build your

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.480
whole order in seconds. You could say something casual like, I want spicy noodles and something

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:43.080
sweet under $10 or send a picture of a burger you saw online. The chat bot finds matching options

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:48.720
right away and adds them to your cart. This works because the AI reads your request the same way it

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:54.940
reads any message and matches it to real items in the app. For students or anyone ordering food

00:00:54.940 --> 00:01:00.580
after a long day, it removes the annoying hunt through categories. It also shows how future apps

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:06.440
might feel more like chatting with a helpful person than filling out forms. If tools like this spread,

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.100
you might soon order almost anything online just by describing what you need. Right now you can

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:18.220
open the DoorDash app on your phone, tap the new Ask DoorDash button at the top, and try typing

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:23.720
a casual request like something cold and fruity for under $5 to see what it suggests.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.340
Okay, now for my favorite part of the show, The Deep Dive, where we look under the hood.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.300
Today's concept is how chat bots turn your casual words into actual results.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:39.260
You know how when you're texting a friend, your phone sometimes guesses the next word before

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:45.100
you finish typing. Now imagine that same auto complete got much better at understanding the whole

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:51.300
sentence you are trying to write, even if you use casual or incomplete words. First it breaks your

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:57.220
message into small pieces it has seen millions of times before, like sorting puzzle pieces into groups,

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:03.720
then it checks what usually comes next in similar messages from its training. The way a recipe tells you

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:09.420
what ingredient follows flower in a cake. Finally it looks at the whole request at once to guess what

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:15.600
you really want, like turning spicy noodles cheap into actual menu items. And that's basically what a

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:21.340
chat bot like Ask DoorDash is doing when it turns your casual words or photo into a food order.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:27.540
It is not reading your mind, but it has seen so many examples of people asking for food that it can

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:33.460
make a smart guess about what matches. So next time someone says natural language understanding,

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:39.280
you can tell them it is basically super powered auto complete that learned from billions of everyday

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:46.320
messages. Not so scary, right? Let's move on to some cool stuff you can try yourself. First up open

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:52.960
AI made a change that helps people who use their coding helper inside chat GPT. Codex is the coding

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:59.200
helper that can write or fix code for you. And now plus pro and business users can bank their rate

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:04.460
limit resets instead of losing them when they expire. Think of rate limits like tickets to a

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:10.480
movie that disappear if you do not use them by a certain date. Now you can save a reset for a busy

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:15.960
day instead of feeling rushed. If you already have one of those plans, go to your account settings

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:22.560
in chat GPT and look for the new option to store resets. Try asking Codex to explain a simple Python

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:27.760
script you found online. Then save the reset for next time you need help with homework or a small

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:34.520
project. Next a free tool from Deezer now scans playlists on Spotify, Apple Music and other

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:41.260
services to spot tracks made by AI. More and more music online is created by computers and you might

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:46.780
want to know what is human made versus machine made. Anyone with a phone can try it without signing

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:52.960
up for Dodger. Go to the Deezer website find the AI detector tool paste a playlist link from another

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:59.180
service and see what it flags. Now for quick bits short stories that caught my eye. A wired

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:05.760
investigation examined Grox image tools in detail. The review found these tools continued to host

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:11.900
sexualized deepfakes of celebrities and public figures. The problematic images remain available

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:18.060
